Hi,

these are Spectronaut's quality scores at different levels (pg = protein group etc).
NA means we treat the values as missing randomly at the imputation step, 0 means missing due to low intensity.
Missing values treatment is described here: https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jproteome.2c00834

Kind regards,
Mateusz

